# Spring AI Handbook

- Target experienced Java/Spring engineers and architects; avoid beginner setup tutorials.
- Preserve every workbook prompt, priority, source type, and key-area mapping in the source manifest.
- Use the portable Spring AI 2.x API surface and flag provider/version-specific behavior.
- Keep probabilistic model decisions separate from deterministic IAM, validation, policy, and transactions.
- Consolidate related prompts into compact topic pages; split only when a major architecture explanation requires it.
- Prefer one flowchart and a concise revision map over repeated answer subsections or code examples.
- Regenerate with `python scripts/build_spring_ai_handbook.py`; hand edits to generated pages will be overwritten.
